                <pb facs="0522" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.001Ubico, Jorge/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-14T12:00:00-07:00">February 14,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. General Ubico took office this morning as constitutional President and
                    received the Diplomatic Corps immediately afterwards.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
